## RULE: Three Readiness Axes (CR / DR / BR)

Every repo has independent progress on three axes. A repo is NEVER "done" by checking only one axis.

### Code Readiness (CR)

| Stage | Pass Criteria |
|-------|--------------|
| CR0 | Not started |
| CR1 | Functionality 100% — zero `NotImplementedError` in core paths; zero stub handlers; no `TODO`/`FIXME` in prod-path code; audit §2 passes |
| CR2 | Unit tests 100% passing — QG unit stage green; coverage ≥ floor (80% libs / 70% services); `--cov-report=xml` written |
| CR3 | Integration tests 100% passing — every direct manifest dependency exercised by an integration test; credential-free (`CLOUD_PROVIDER=local CLOUD_MOCK_MODE=true`) |
| CR4 | Quality gate passing locally — `bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` Pass 1 green; 0 ruff errors; 0 basedpyright errors; no bypass shortcuts added |
| CR5 | Quickmerge to feature branch — CI passes on `feat/code-readiness-<repo>` or equivalent |

**CR3 manifest rule:** Count the repo's `dependencies[]` in `workspace-manifest.json`. Each dep must appear in
`tests/integration/`. Repos with zero manifest dependencies satisfy CR3 automatically.

### Deployment Readiness (DR)

| Stage | Pass Criteria |
|-------|--------------|
| DR0 | Not started |
| DR1 | Docker builds; cloudbuild.yaml correct; infra provisioned; `setup-workspace.sh` succeeds |
| DR2 | CI smoke tests pass — `production_mock_e2e` GHA suite green; zero live calls; emulators only |
| DR3 | Feature environment deployed — `GET /health` 200; `GET /readiness` 200; smoke route returns expected payload |
| DR4 | Staging SIT pass — system-integration-tests full suite green; no circuit breaker trips during run |
| DR5 | Load/performance pass — P99 latency ≤ SLA; no memory leaks; throughput ≥ target |
| DR6 | Production-ready — zero CRITICAL CVEs; auth middleware verified; runbook in `docs/`; ≥24 hr health post-deploy |

### Business Readiness (BR)

| Stage | Pass Criteria |
|-------|--------------|
| BR0 | Not started |
| BR1 | Acceptance criteria defined in the owning plan |
| BR2 | Circuit breaker validated (fault injection + 3-state machine). **N/A for libraries and UIs.** |
| BR3 | Event handling validated — all UEI events fire; schema matches UAC canonical; correlation_id propagated |
| BR4 | PnL/performance targets met — domain KPIs measured; declare "N/A" with reason for non-revenue repos |
| BR5 | PnL optimization validated — backtest confirms positive contribution; artifacts in GCS. Revenue repos only. |
| BR6 | Batch vs live validation — t+1 check passes within tolerance |
| BR7 | Staging vs live parity — N-minute replay within tolerance |
| BR8 | **User approved** — human sign-off. **No agent may set BR8 autonomously.** |

---

## RULE: v1.0.0 Requires Specific Axis Minimums

A repo CANNOT be promoted to v1.0.0 unless:
- CR5 (merged to `main` via cascade — not just `feat/*`)
- DR3 (has shipped to feature environment at least once)
- DR4 (staging SIT passed)
- BR2 (circuit breaker — services only)
- BR3 (event handling — all repos that emit UEI events)
- BR4 (performance targets measured and met)
- BR8 (user approved — no exceptions)

Full gate table: `unified-trading-pm/docs/REPO_READINESS_CHECKLIST.md § v1.0.0 Gate`

---

## RULE: Every Undone Item Must Have a Plan

Before claiming a repo is v1.0.0 eligible, EVERY unmet checklist item must be tracked in an active plan
(in `plans/active/`) with a completion timeline. If an item is declared N/A, the reason must appear in the plan's
`repo_gates` `readiness_note` field. No silent gaps.

---

## RULE: Agent Semver Limits

| Bump | Agent can auto-approve? | Conditions |
|------|------------------------|------------|
| patch (0.x.y → 0.x.y+1) | Yes | CR4 at time of merge; CI auto-bumps via `version-bump.yml` |
| minor (0.x.y → 0.x+1.0) | Yes | CR5 (CI on feat branch passed); no FAIL items in audit |
| minor breaking (feat!:) | Yes | CR5 + DR2 (CI smoke); must use `--to-staging` path |
| **1.0.0** | **No — user required** | All axes met + BR8 (user approval) |

---

## RULE: Code Readiness Master Plan Is the Tracker

`plans/archive/code_readiness_master_plan_2026_03_11.plan.md` is the authoritative per-repo CR/DR/BR state tracker
for all 65 repos. Do NOT track individual repo readiness in ad-hoc comments or chat — update the master plan.

Active sub-plans (phase2_library_tier_hardening, phase3_service_hardening_integration, etc.) align to the master
plan. They contain the actual implementation todos. The master plan tracks aggregate stage state.

---

## RULE: Tier Blocking (Readiness Promotion Only)

The tier-blocking invariant applies to readiness promotion (not day-to-day development):

```
T0 all CR5+DR3 → T1 promotion unblocked
T0+T1 all CR5+DR3 → T2 promotion unblocked
T0+T1+T2 all CR5+DR3 → T3 promotion unblocked
T3 CR5+DR3 → Services (T4) promotion unblocked
T4 CR5+DR4 → APIs (T5) promotion unblocked
T5 CR5+DR4 → UIs (T6) promotion unblocked
```

WHY: Tier N cannot be verified against a broken Tier N-1. Promoting a T2 repo before T1 is CR5+DR3 means
integration tests at T2 are testing against an unreleased T1.

